IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`
IMPORT `pip-part7-periods`

-- Tests of regulation 32. Expected values were worked out by hand from the text before the file was run.

§ `Tests of regulation 32(1) to (3)`

#ASSERT `reg 32(1): C is in a period of residence` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 32(1): C is in a period of residence` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 32(1): C is in a period of residence` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 32(1): C is in a period of residence` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- C enters on 10 March 2025 and leaves on 2 April 2025: the period begins on 11 March and ends on 1 April.
#ASSERT `reg 32(2)(a): the first day of the period of residence` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 3 11
#ASSERT `reg 32(2)(b) and (3): the last day of the period of residence` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 2) `with` FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 4 1
-- Another period follows immediately: the earlier period ends on the day C leaves.
#ASSERT `reg 32(2)(b) and (3): the last day of the period of residence` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 2) `with` TRUE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 4 2
-- The first day of a month and the last day of a month.
#ASSERT `reg 32(2)(a): the first day of the period of residence` (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 3 1
#ASSERT `reg 32(2)(b) and (3): the last day of the period of residence` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) `with` FALSE EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 2 28
`the March stay` MEANS `reg 32(2) and (3): the period of residence from entry to leaving` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) `to` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 2) `with` FALSE
#ASSERT (`the March stay`)'s `the first day of the period of residence` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 3 11
#ASSERT (`the March stay`)'s `the last day of the period of residence` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 4 1
-- 11 to 31 March is 21 days and 1 April makes 22.
#ASSERT `reg 32(2): the days of the period of residence` `the March stay` EQUALS 22
-- Entering and leaving on the same day: no days.
#ASSERT `reg 32(2): the days of the period of residence` (`reg 32(2) and (3): the period of residence from entry to leaving` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) `to` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) `with` FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- Leaving the next day: no days of residence (entry day and leaving day are both outside it).
#ASSERT `reg 32(2): the days of the period of residence` (`reg 32(2) and (3): the period of residence from entry to leaving` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) `to` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 11) `with` FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- Leaving two days later: one day.
#ASSERT `reg 32(2): the days of the period of residence` (`reg 32(2) and (3): the period of residence from entry to leaving` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) `to` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 12) `with` FALSE) EQUALS 1

§ `Tests of regulation 32(4) and (5): the interval`

-- The earlier period ends on 1 April 2025. A later period beginning on 30 April has the 28 days 2 to 29 April between: joined.
#ASSERT `reg 32(4)(a) and (5): the interval between the periods does not exceed the limit` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) `and` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 30) `with` FALSE
-- Beginning on 1 May: 29 days between: not joined.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 32(4)(a) and (5): the interval between the periods does not exceed the limit` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) `and` (YearMonthDay 2025 5 1) `with` FALSE)
-- Beginning the day after: no interval.
#ASSERT `reg 32(4)(a) and (5): the interval between the periods does not exceed the limit` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) `and` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 2) `with` FALSE
-- Both periods of imprisonment or detention: one year. The interval 2 April 2025 to 1 April 2026 is a year; a later period beginning 2 April 2026 is joined, one beginning 3 April 2026 is not.
#ASSERT `reg 32(4)(a) and (5): the interval between the periods does not exceed the limit` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) `and` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 2) `with` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 32(4)(a) and (5): the interval between the periods does not exceed the limit` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) `and` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 3) `with` TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 32(4)(a) and (5): the interval between the periods does not exceed the limit` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) `and` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) `with` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 32(4)(a) and (5): the interval between the periods does not exceed the limit` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) `and` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) `with` FALSE)

§ `Tests of regulation 32(4): the continuous period`

-- P1 11 March to 1 April 2025 (22 days). P2 29 April to 10 May (2 + 10 = 12 days), after an interval of 27 days: joined.
`the first period` MEANS `a period of residence` OF YearMonthDay 2025 3 11, YearMonthDay 2025 4 1
`the second period, after 27 days` MEANS `a period of residence` OF YearMonthDay 2025 4 29, YearMonthDay 2025 5 10
`the second period, after 28 days` MEANS `a period of residence` OF YearMonthDay 2025 4 30, YearMonthDay 2025 5 10
`the second period, after 29 days` MEANS `a period of residence` OF YearMonthDay 2025 5 1, YearMonthDay 2025 5 10
-- 22 + 12 = 34 days on 10 May; 22 + 3 = 25 on 1 May.
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the second period, after 27 days`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 5 10) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 34
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the second period, after 27 days`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 5 1) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 25
-- An interval of 28 days is joined: 22 + 11 = 33. An interval of 29 days is not: 10 days alone.
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the second period, after 28 days`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 5 10) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 33
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the second period, after 29 days`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 5 10) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 10
-- A day in the first period counts that period only up to the day: 11 March to 20 March is 10 days.
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the second period, after 27 days`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 10
-- The first day and the last day of the first period.
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 11) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 22
-- A day in no period: the interval between them, or before the first, or after the last.
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the second period, after 27 days`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 15) `with` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) `with` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 2) `with` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` EMPTY `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 2) `with` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Three periods joined in a row: 22 + 12 + (a third, 1 June to 10 June after 21 days: 10 days) = 44.
`the third period` MEANS `a period of residence` OF YearMonthDay 2025 6 1, YearMonthDay 2025 6 10
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the second period, after 27 days`, `the third period`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 44
-- A break after the second: the third alone. The third period begins 10 June after the second ends 10 May: 29 days between (11 May to 9 June): not joined.
`the late third period` MEANS `a period of residence` OF YearMonthDay 2025 6 10, YearMonthDay 2025 6 12
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the second period, after 27 days`, `the late third period`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 12) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 3
-- Section 87 periods: one year. P1 11 March to 1 April 2025 (22 days); P2 31 December 2025 to 5 January 2026 (6 days): 22 + 6 = 28.
`the prison stay after nine months` MEANS `a period of residence` OF YearMonthDay 2025 12 31, YearMonthDay 2026 1 5
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the prison stay after nine months`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) `with` TRUE EQUALS JUST 28
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the prison stay after nine months`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) `with` FALSE EQUALS JUST 6
-- The year's boundary: a second period beginning 2 April 2026 joins (22 + 4 = 26 to 5 April), one beginning 3 April does not (3 days to 5 April).
`the prison stay after exactly a year` MEANS `a period of residence` OF YearMonthDay 2026 4 2, YearMonthDay 2026 4 5
`the prison stay after a year and a day` MEANS `a period of residence` OF YearMonthDay 2026 4 3, YearMonthDay 2026 4 5
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the prison stay after exactly a year`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 5) `with` TRUE EQUALS JUST 26
#ASSERT `reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` (LIST `the first period`, `the prison stay after a year and a day`) `up to` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 5) `with` TRUE EQUALS JUST 3
